---
/**
 * p63 · Pane
 *
 * A single piece of blue glass, cut landscape, with nothing behind it.
 *
 * The four Plozz studies here share two silhouettes and vary only the light.
 * This one and p66 are the same 28x20 pane with the same [3, 1] corner cut;
 * p64 and p65 are the same 26x22 faceplate with the same [4, 2, 1] cut. Reuse
 * the shape, change the physics, and the comparison is about the physics.
 *
 * A pane leaning back under a light that is above it, not beside it, does not
 * shade like a button. The top three rings run near-white and step down one
 * stop at a time until they meet the field; the left is quiet, one stop and
 * then nothing, because a vertical edge turned toward a high light catches
 * almost none of it; and the bottom carries the glass's own thickness as a
 * deep rim, three rings falling from the darkest blue in the scale back up to
 * the field. The right does the same in half the range. The mitres land on the
 * true 45 because the facet is chosen by whichever edge is nearest, ties going
 * to the top and then the left.
 *
 * That asymmetry is the whole argument against the disc. A circle shaded this
 * way is a sphere; a rectangle shaded this way is a sheet of glass, and a
 * sheet of glass in landscape is a screen even with no frame drawn around it.
 *
 * Nothing is cleared for the letterforms. The four inner rings resolve to one
 * flat field a full pixel wider than the face on every side, so the ZZ sits on
 * plain glass with the ramp beginning outside it: 6 rows of air above the face
 * and 6 below, 10 columns either side, measured. Face ink is the keyline
 * colour, as Hozz does it.
 *
 * 10 tones off the family blue, 12.6:1 at the face.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { faceBoxAt, facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
const face = { cx: 16, cy: 16, size: 'md', smile: 'compact', gap: 2 } as const;
const box = faceBoxAt(face);
if (box.x !== 12 || box.y !== 12 || box.right !== 19 || box.bottom !== 19) {
  throw new Error(`p63 face geometry changed: ${JSON.stringify(box)}`);
}
---

